Inspect the current repository state before acting. Determine whether the user wants each applicable action, asking one question at a time:

- version change;
- changelog entry;
- final validation;
- commit;
- pull request.

Do not assume every feature needs every action. Do not include unrelated working-tree changes in a commit. Never overwrite user work, rewrite history, force-push, or publish anything without explicit authorization.

Perform authorized actions in a safe order and report exactly what was done, skipped, or left for the user, including the final repository state.
